hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27794","Haddathana Abd al-Samad who said: Haddathana Hammam who said: Haddathana Amir al-Ahwal who said: Haddathana Makhul: Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz that Abu Mahdhura told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him the adhan in nineteen phrases and the iqama in seventeen phrases: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah; and the iqama doubled doubled without tarji."
"27795","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid who said: Haddathana Hudhayl ibn Bilal from Ibn Abi Mahdhura from his father or from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the adhan for us and for our freedmen, and the watering for Banu Hashim, and the veiling for Banu Abd al-Dar."
